package <%= basePackage %>.<%= module %>.domain.contract

import <%= basePackage %>.platform.kernel.Command

/**
 * Asks the <%= module %> context to handle [subject].
 *
 * **Rename me.** `keel add module <%= module %>` knows this context's
 * *name* and nothing about what it is for, so it cannot invent a use
 * case. This is a stand-in with the right shape — a command in, a
 * result or a rejection out — and replacing it with your first real
 * use case is meant to be the first thing you do here.
 *
 * What is *not* a placeholder is the structure around it: the
 * command/result pair, the rejection this context owns, and the fact
 * that nothing in this module names another bounded context.
 *
 * @property subject what this use case acts on — deliberately
 *   anonymous, which is what a placeholder can honestly call the thing
 *   it was handed.
 */
data class <%= Module %>Command(val subject: String) : Command<<%= Module %>Result>
